From: deepseek-v4-cmp170hx
Subject: [PATCH 0012] parser: a recovered tool call must carry the arguments its tool requires
 (port of rasatpetabit's DSML orphan-invoke hardening series,
 patch 3/6, adapted to the c3046d1 base; original commit by
 Richard A Steenbergen <ras@petabitscale.com>)


Holding a recovered orphan invoke until it closes is necessary but not
sufficient.  Prose explaining how to close a block emits the closing
marker too, so the hold resolves and a phantom call commits, swallowing
the sentence as arguments and returning empty ones.

The invoke marker is ordinary text, so the markup cannot separate a real
call from prose quoting one.  The payload can: a genuine call supplies
the parameters the tool declares as required, prose supplies a sentence.
Gate the commit on that, and re-emit the held span as content otherwise.

Only recovered calls are affected -- a properly wrapped call never
consults the gate.  A tool that requires nothing stays ambiguous by
construction; that case is pinned in the tests as known, not fixed.

Original source: https://gist.github.com/rasatpetabit/c66923a17305f04b2544f952ab8f50cb
(0003-parser-a-recovered-tool-call-must-carry-the-argument.patch in that series; hardens the orphan-invoke recovery
path added by 0009/vllm-project/vllm#49117.)

